// Files what would have been sent into /CaughtMail instead of delivering it, so that email can be
// exercised without a mail server. It outranks Sling's own mail service rather than replacing it.
//
// Shipped everywhere and inert everywhere, because the component requires a configuration to
// activate and this feature supplies none. What switches it on is `dev/email-catcher-enabled.json`,
// which only the test and demo aggregates include. One set of artifacts, and the difference between
// environments is a configuration a deployment can read rather than a bundle list it has to trust.
{
    "prototype":{
        "id": "${project.groupId}:iap-email-catcher:slingosgifeature:${project.version}"
    }
}
